# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5
# An output leaves the run alone (#233): in the deterministic mode the run
# with `[output] observables`, the free-energy file, the pull file, an energy
# file, and a trajectory ends in the state of the run without them, bit for
# bit, with the rows of its log, at constant energy, at constant
# temperature, and under NPT with the barostat of Trotter type, in mixed
# precision on the CPU. The same with `rebuild_interval`, and for the rows
# of the log at the end only (D204). A Python simulation whose parts are
# read between them, or that has reporters, ends in the state of one that is
# not read.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/output_independence.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU mdir %t Mixed NVE NVT NPT-TROTTER | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: CPU Mixed NVE: {{[0-9]+}} builds of the neighbor structure in 40 steps
# CHECK-SAME: compared files, rows-at-end
# CHECK: CPU Mixed NVT: {{[0-9]+}} builds
# CHECK-SAME: compared files, rows-at-end
# CHECK: CPU Mixed NPT-TROTTER: {{[0-9]+}} builds
# CHECK-SAME: compared observables, free_energy, pull, files, interval-files, rows-at-end
# CHECK: CPU Mixed mdir run: the outputs leave the final state and the rows of the log as they are without them, in 3 ensembles
# CHECK: CPU Mixed Python: state() and view() between the parts and the reporters
# CHECK: output independence passed
